UPDATE "search_candidates" SET "exec_id" = 99, "notes" = 'harm_finding=1: the title poses its own question as whether disabled people are being DENIED rights, so it is an inadequacy study by construction, and R7 makes that first-class evidence rather than a by-product. WHY THIS CLUSTER MATTERS MORE THAN ANY SINGLE ITEM: REF-01006''s reference list contains at least five accessibility-audit studies of Indian and Brazilian health facilities (bb0030 Pinto 2021 Brazil national audit doi 10.3390/ijerph18062953; bb0100 Singh 2024 New Delhi hospitals doi 10.32388/M7E7KE.3; this one; bb0110 Sharma 2025 Gwalior; bb0130 Mohapatra 2024 Delphi on public buildings doi 10.12688/f1000research.156920.1). If any of them tabulates measured gradients, the corpus gains something it has almost none of: what ramps in the world ACTUALLY measure, as against what codes require or what laboratory studies test. || RESOLVED 2026-09-25 (R15, re-described from the source): NOT ADMITTED: THE BODY COULD NOT BE READ FROM THIS ENVIRONMENT, AND THE PREMISE THAT IT WAS OPEN ACCESS AND RETRIEVABLE IS CORRECTED. Batch 19 and the batch-20 runbook both described this as ''DOI-bearing, open access, retrievable''. It is FREE TO READ at PubMed Central (PMC11116980; OpenAlex and Unpaywall both call it green OA with PMC as the only location) but NOT OPEN-ACCESS LICENSED: NCBI efetch returns front matter only, carrying the comment ''The publisher of this article does not allow downloading of the full text in XML form'', and its pmc-prop-open-access flag is ''no''. ROUTES TRIED THIS BATCH, EACH PERSISTED IN THE RETRIEVAL LOG: Crossref record (200, metadata and a 16-entry deposited reference list); Europe PMC core record (200, abstract); Europe PMC fullTextXML (HTTP 500); NCBI efetch db=pmc (200, front matter only, XML withheld by publisher); pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov article page and its /pdf/ (200 but a reCAPTCHA ''Checking your browser'' interstitial, no article); Europe PMC PDF render (403, Cloudflare ''Just a moment''); ScienceDirect PII S0377123722001952 (403, Cloudflare error 1000); Unpaywall and OpenAlex (200, no location other than PMC). WHAT THE ABSTRACT SAYS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT: a 30-day hospital-based cross-sectional audit of one health care institution of national importance in India against the Central Public Works Department (CPWD) checklist -- ''Out of total 126 pointers, 45 pointers were found to be totally compliant, 30 pointers were found to be partially compliant, and remaining 51 pointers were found to be not applicable''. IT DOES NOT SAY whether a ramp gradient is one of the 126 pointers or how any ramp scored, so the staged claim that this document type ''measures ramp gradients in a table'' is UNTESTED for this item, not confirmed. harm_finding=1 stands on the abstract''s own conclusion (''important gaps in accessibility''). NOT QUEUED FOR ANYONE: the text is readable in an ordinary browser at PMC, which is a different situation from the three items the owner ruled exhausted on 2026-09-25, so this row is left PENDING rather than marked exhausted -- but no retrieval task is assigned to any person. || RESOLVED 2026-09-25 (R15, re-described from the source): STAYS PENDING-VERIFICATION, DELIBERATELY, NOW THAT EXHAUSTED EXISTS (migration 096, owner ruling 2026-09-25). EXHAUSTED is for an item to which no route exists from anywhere. This one has a route: PubMed Central serves it free to read (Unpaywall and OpenAlex both give is_oa true, green, via PMC), and what stopped batch 20 -- a reCAPTCHA interstitial and Cloudflare 403s -- is a barrier to this environment''s automated requests, which may be transient. The owner''s ruling drew exactly this distinction. Not queued for anyone, and no request is drafted.

